# 4. Coding Principles

## Functions

Small · single responsibility · target 20–40 lines.

## Nesting

Maximum two levels. Prefer early return.

## Naming

Business terminology only.

Good: `organizationId`, `memberId`, `eventDefinition`  
Bad: `tmp`, `obj`, `foo`, `data`

## Magic Numbers

Never. Always define named constants.

## Error Handling

Never ignore errors. Never use empty catch blocks. Return meaningful errors.

## Boolean Arguments

Avoid `createUser(true)`. Prefer `createAdministrator()`.

## Pure Functions

Prefer pure functions. Minimize side effects.

## Immutability

Prefer immutable data. Mutation must be intentional.

